{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"kind":"article","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Origami to SwiftUI reference","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What each Origami patch becomes in SwiftUI, so you know which construct — or which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" helper — to reach for."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI both describe how values flow and change over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time, so the translations map onto SwiftUI’s own tools: computed properties for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pure math, gestures and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" for interaction, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" for motion. Most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patches land on a native SwiftUI construct. A few need a helper from the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library, named after the patch it stands in for."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Patch → SwiftUI","anchor":"Patch-%E2%86%92-SwiftUI","type":"heading"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami patch","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftUI","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure value patch (Add, interpolate, logic)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"computed property \/ expression (native)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction (Tap, Press, Double Tap, Long Press)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"gesture + ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View\/interaction(down:position:onTap:onDoubleTap:onLongPress:)"},{"text":" (helper)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — Drag"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"drag(enable:momentum:bounds:position:translation:velocity:reset:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (helper)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Magnification \/ Pinch"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MagnifyGesture"},{"type":"text","text":" (native)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.PopSwitch"},{"type":"text","text":" — Pop Switch"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" flipped on a threshold, ","type":"text"},{"code":".spring","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pop (native)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"builtin.layer.shape"},{"type":"text","text":" — Shape (triangle)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/RoundedTriangle","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (helper)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State \/ memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" + update logic (native)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop \/ Spring)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(.spring)"},{"type":"text","text":" (native)"}]}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI "},{"code":"View","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" body."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"How the categories map","anchor":"How-the-categories-map","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure value patches"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"Add","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", interpolation, logic — carry no state. They run an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"input through math and emit a result, which is exactly a computed property or an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inline expression.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" exposes discrete outputs: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"down"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"position"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onTap"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDoubleTap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onLongPress"},{"type":"text","text":". Each becomes a SwiftUI gesture whose result lands in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" or fires a callback. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".interaction(…)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier attaches only the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recognizers you ask for, so gesture arbitration stays clean."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"State and memory","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"code":"Switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Sample and Hold","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Pop Switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — remember a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between evaluations. That is what "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is for; the update path is a gesture"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"callback, an "},{"code":".onChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or an assignment."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Animation","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"code":"Classic Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Pop Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — drives a value toward a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"target over time, which is a state change wrapped in "},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(_:value:)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"One naming note: Origami’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Transition","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" means ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"interpolation"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" (mapping one range","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"onto another), not SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".transition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier for view insertion and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"removal.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"When a mapping isn’t exact","level":2,"anchor":"When-a-mapping-isnt-exact"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Some Origami semantics have no direct SwiftUI equivalent — continuous-time springs,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"custom JavaScript patches, absolute-position layout. Rather than approximate them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"silently, each translated view marks the gap with an inline ","type":"text"},{"code":"TODO","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in its source,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so the caveat travels with the code. The individual pattern pages link to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"source where those notes live.","type":"text"}]}]}],"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"Swami","url":"\/documentation\/swami","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami patterns, rebuilt as SwiftUI you can read — each one a worked example of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patches behind it, so you can see how a prototype’s behavior is written and reach for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same patch on your own layers."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/RoundedTriangle":{"title":"RoundedTriangle","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RoundedTriangle"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/RoundedTriangle","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RoundedTriangle"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/roundedtriangle","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An upward-pointing triangle with uniformly rounded corners.","type":"text"}]}}}